{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Auralization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Auralization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"auralization auralization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Auralization.md","fileName":"Auralization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Auralization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[XR Display Systems]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Display Systems","Spatial Audio","Auditory Display","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Auralization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Auralization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"auralization auralization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Auralization.md","fileName":"Auralization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Auralization","heading":"Auralization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Auralization renders the sound field of a source in space to simulate a binaural listening experience. It attempts to recreate how sound travels and reflects through an environment, making it useful for reverberation.\n\nWave-based methods solve or approximate the sound-wave equation. Ray-based methods follow paths from source to listener but simplify effects associated with wavelength. Ambisonics records a spherical directional sound field, while wave-field synthesis approximates virtual sources by combining many physical loudspeakers.\n\nAuralization is one route to producing [[Spatial Audio]] for an [[Auditory Display]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["XR Display Systems","Spatial Audio","Auditory Display","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Auralization.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Auralization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sour